@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g6-nouns.l4: the nouns that G6's modules share (Chapter 6, ss.41-57, and the Third Schedule).
-- DECLARE only: no rule and no #EVAL.  domain.l4 carries Party, Person, Violation and Listed violation,
-- and G6 does not edit it; the records below are G6's own because they are the notice, the demand and
-- the warning of Chapter 6, which no other group needs (PLAN section 8).
-- The test for membership is the one domain.l4 states: could a witness of ordinary competence testify
-- to the fact?  What the Law makes of the fact (is the notice good, is the amount owed) is a rule.
-- "Delivered on" is the day the Law's word "mesira" (delivery) names; the Law does not say how a
-- document is delivered, so the day is an input.
-- Facts the Law leaves to the Commissioner's opinion or discretion (reasonable grounds, special reasons,
-- intention to impose) are INPUTS to the rules, never fields here.

§ `Chapter 6, ss.41-57: the nouns G6's modules share`

-- Column A of the Third Schedule ends each item with the provision it says was contravened.
-- Items (1) and (2) both name section 3(a); items (5) and (6) both name section 18(a).
@desc The provision of the Law that a Third Schedule item says was contravened (the last clause of column A of each item)
DECLARE `Provision contravened` IS ONE OF
    `contravenes section 3(a)`
    `contravenes section 4`
    `contravenes section 13`
    `contravenes section 18(a)`
    `contravenes section 31(2)`

@desc One row of the Third Schedule: the item, the violation, the provision it contravenes, and column B for an individual and for a corporation; a dash in the Law is NOTHING here
DECLARE `Third Schedule row` HAS
    `the item number` IS A NUMBER @desc The number in parentheses that opens column A
    `the listed violation` IS A `Listed violation` @desc The violation column A describes
    `the provision contravened` IS A `Provision contravened` @desc The provision column A names at its end
    `column B for an individual` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The amount in new shekels in the individual column; NOTHING where the Law prints a dash
    `column B for a corporation` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The amount in new shekels in the corporation column; NOTHING where the Law prints a dash

@desc An earlier violation by a person, with what s.45(b) asks of it: whether a sanction was imposed for it or the person was convicted of it
DECLARE `Previous violation` HAS
    `the violator` IS A Person @desc Who committed the earlier violation
    `the listed violation` IS A `Listed violation` @desc Which Third Schedule item the earlier act breached
    `date of the act` IS A DATE @desc The day the earlier act was committed
    `a financial sanction was imposed for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if a financial sanction was imposed on the violator for the earlier violation
    `the violator was convicted for it` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the violator was convicted of an offence for the earlier violation

@desc An extension of a period that the Commissioner may grant under s.43 or s.53(b): the day the period now ends and whether the special reasons were recorded
DECLARE `Extension granted by the Commissioner` HAS
    `the period now ends on` IS A DATE @desc The last day of the period as the Commissioner extended it; an official's choice, never computed
    `special reasons were recorded` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Commissioner recorded special reasons for the extension

@desc The notice of intention to impose a financial sanction (s.42): when it was delivered and what it states
DECLARE `Notice of intention` HAS
    `delivered on` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was delivered to the violator
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice is in writing
    `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice states the act or omission and when the breach was committed (s.42(b)(1))
    `states the amount of the sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice states the amount of the financial sanction (s.42(b)(2))
    `the period for payment the notice states, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The period for payment the notice states (s.42(b)(2)); NOTHING if the notice states none
    `states the violator's right to make representations under section 43` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice states the right to make representations (s.42(b)(3))
    `states that the notice will be treated as a payment demand if the right is not used` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice states the consequence of s.44(d) (s.42(b)(3))
    `states the power to add for a continuing or repeat violation and the rate of the addition` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice states the power under s.45 and the rate of the addition (s.42(b)(4))
    `states the intention to publish the violator's name` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice announces an intention to publish an individual violator's name (s.57(c)); not required by s.42(b)

@desc A payment demand (s.44(b)(1)): when it was delivered and what it states
DECLARE `Payment demand` HAS
    `delivered on` IS A DATE @desc The day the demand was delivered to the violator
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the demand is in writing
    `states the updated amount of the sanction` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the demand states the amount of the sanction as updated (s.44(b)(1))
    `the period for payment the demand states, in days` IS A MAYBE NUMBER @desc The period for payment the demand states (s.44(b)(1)); NOTHING if the demand states none
    `states the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the demand details the reasons for the decision (s.44(c))

@desc A written notice that the Commissioner decided not to impose a financial sanction (s.44(b)(2))
DECLARE `Notice of a decision not to impose a sanction` HAS
    `delivered on` IS A DATE @desc The day the notice was delivered to the violator
    `in writing` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice is in writing
    `states the reasons for the decision` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the notice details the reasons for the decision (s.44(c))

@desc An administrative warning given instead of a financial sanction (s.52)
DECLARE `Administrative warning` HAS
    `the violator` IS A Person @desc To whom the warning was given
    `the listed violation the warning concerns` IS A `Listed violation` @desc Which Third Schedule item the warning concerns; the provision it concerns follows from the item
    `delivered on` IS A DATE @desc The day the warning was delivered to the violator
    `states the act or omission that is the breach and the date of the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the warning states the act or omission and when it was committed (s.52(b))
    `tells the violator to stop the breach` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the warning informs the violator that the breach must stop (s.52(b))
    `warns of a sanction for a continuing or repeat violation` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the warning informs the violator that continuing or repeating the breach exposes the violator to a sanction under s.45 (s.52(b))
    `states the violator's right to ask for cancellation under section 53` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the warning states the right to ask for its cancellation (s.52(b))
    `cancelled under section 53` IS A BOOLEAN @desc True if the Commissioner cancelled the warning on a request under s.53

@desc The two grounds s.53(a) allows for a request to cancel an administrative warning
DECLARE `Ground for cancelling a warning` IS ONE OF
    `the violator did not commit the breach`                                                   -- s.53(a)(1)
    `the act the violator committed, as detailed in the warning, is not a breach`              -- s.53(a)(2)

@desc What the Commissioner decided on a request to cancel an administrative warning (s.53(c))
DECLARE `Decision on a request to cancel a warning` IS ONE OF
    `to cancel the warning`
    `to refuse the request and leave the warning in place`

@desc Whether the Commissioner decided to impose a financial sanction after considering the representations (s.44(a)); the decision itself is the Commissioner's discretion and an input
DECLARE `Decision on a financial sanction` IS ONE OF
    `to impose the financial sanction`
    `not to impose a financial sanction`
